  "$comment_u5a": "Client parser cases added in. parserCases: synthetic bodies; images[] compare kind, mime, value, revisedPrompt in order; value is the raw b64 string, the URL, or the full data URL. Any URL field starting with data: (case-insensitive) is kind data_url, mime from its prefix lowercased. metaExpect: for every real sample, usage = {inputTokens, outputTokens, totalTokens} taken per field from usage.input_tokens / usage.prompt_tokens / usageMetadata.promptTokenCount (output: output_tokens / completion_tokens / candidatesTokenCount; total: total_tokens / totalTokenCount), first positive integer wins, else the first integer present, else null; usage = null when all three are null; declaredSize from top-level size \"WxH\", else usage.width + usage.height; informational only, real size always comes from decodeImageInfo. decodeCases: decodeImageInfo(bytes) reads the pixel size from the image header (raw stored size, EXIF orientation ignored), png / jpeg / webp (VP8, VP8L, VP8X) only, anything else or truncated returns null (= decode_failed). fetchPolicy + fetchCases: URL images are downloaded right away; failure kinds use image_error_samples.v1 names. assembleCases: per-image outcomes → result. Review round: numbers count when the JSON value is integral (14.0 = 14, \"14\" and 1.5 do not); size \"WxH\" is digits only and both > 0; declared mime is read only for b64 items (url items: null); data URL mime only from a data:image/<x>;base64, prefix, otherwise null; inlineData that is not an object falls back to inline_data; png width / height must be 1..2^31-1; jpeg SOF segment length must be >= 7. metaCases: synthetic usage / declaredSize. materializeCases: base64 accepts whitespace and missing padding, rejects any other non-alphabet character (URL-safe included); data URLs need ;base64,; the decoded mime wins over the declared one.",
